    ('05133e1e-6d12-461c-a682-d8ac77d2550f'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:05133e1e-6d12-461c-a682-d8ac77d2550f:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''4'' restored on Necropolis of Pranu Muttedu', 'f46608c1158c0e02dd91ddb030ccff5c', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Necropolis/tombs complex'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 47 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:32999", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0011:chunk-0001: description ''The Necropolis of Pranu Muttedu near Goni in southern Sardinia is one of the most important pre-Nuragic funerary complexes on the island, spanning a 200,000 sq m park. Dating to the Late Neolithic Ozieri culture through the early Copper Age, it contains the highest concentration of menhirs in Sardinia -- about 60 proto-anthropomorphic standing stones arranged in pairs and groups. The complex includes megalithic tombs, a Domus de Janas necropolis at Genna Accas with stone circles, dolmens at Baccoi, and round buildings of probable sacral character. Excavations by Enrico Atzeni began in 1980.'' -> \"The necropolis of Pranu Muttedu is one of the most important funerary areas of pre-Nuragic Sardinia and is located near Goni [1]. The complex features a high concentration of menhirs—around sixty—second only to the vast site of Biru ''e Concas in Sorgono, where roughly 200 menhirs have been recorded [1]. These are arranged in pairs, alignments, or groups [1]. Other monuments include funerary chambers of various types, originally covered by a tumulus and enclosed within megalithic circles built with stone blocks arranged in concentric rings [1]. The area also contains several domus de janas [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
