    ('14dd917b-b58e-45d6-9578-bc1cefd34728'::uuid, 'antiquity', '8', '7', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:14dd917b-b58e-45d6-9578-bc1cefd34728:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: antiquity ''7'' restored on Mochlos', 'a3e97d7444ca16bdde683fa7164f9977', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 8 from period_start -3100"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28934", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0216:chunk-0001: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-3100''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30350", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33135", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0015:chunk-0001: description ''Mochlos (3100 BC–10th c. AD) is a small island in the Gulf of Mirabello, eastern Crete, with ruins of a Minoan settlement[1]. Evidence suggests it was connected to the mainland in Minoan times, serving as an eastern harbor[1]. American archaeologist Richard Seager excavated the site in 1908, uncovering a prepalatial cemetery with tombs, pithos burials, and pit graves at the western end[2][3].'' -> ''Mochlos is a small, uninhabited island in the Gulf of Mirabello in eastern Crete, and the archaeological site of an ancient Minoan settlement [1]. There is evidence that Mochlos was not an island in Minoan times, but was attached to the mainland and acted as an eastern harbor [1]. Mochlos was first excavated by Richard Seager in 1908 at the western end of the island, where a prepalatial cemetery was found [1]. The cemetery was in use from Early Minoan I to Middle Minoan IA [1]. Ten Late Minoan I metal hoards were recently excavated at Mochlos [1]. Lead isotope analyses indicate that copper oxhide ingots and fragments from these hoards originated in Cyprus [1]. Large quantities of Early Minoan gold jewelry were excavated at Mochlos in 1908 and are on display in the Heraklion Museum [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
