 Pallenis and - probably - Apollo [1]. The temple was transferred to the Agora and rededicated to Ares during the reign of Augustus [1]. Around 230 fragments of the superstructure have been found reused in later structures throughout the Agora [1]. They are now collected at the western end of the temple [1]. They are made of a distinctive crystalline Pentelic marble with gray-green chlorite veins [1]. They can be dated stylistically to the second half of the 5th century BC, probably the 430s BC [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('159db30a-1599-4425-8134-e0d08d164a95'::uuid, 'antiquity', '10', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:159db30a-1599-4425-8134-e0d08d164a95:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: antiquity ''4'' restored on Le Regourdou', '7d427b7c131f98c41a150aa29588f655', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 10 from period_start -68000"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28260", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0101:chunk-0001: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-68000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30352", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43323", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0072:chunk-0001: description ''Regourdou is a cave structure in Dordogne, France, located 800 meters from the famous Lascaux cave complex [1]. The site consists of a collapsed ancient karst cavity measuring 35 meters deep [1]. Excavations yielded well-preserved Neanderthal fossils that may represent intentional burials [1]. The current excavation team states the correct name is \"Regourdou\" rather than the commonly used \"Le Régourdou\" [1].'' -> ''Le Regourdou is an archaeological site in the Dordogne department, France, on top of a hill just 800 m from the famous cave complex of Lascaux [1]. At this now collapsed 35 m deep ancient karst cavity remarkably well preserved Neanderthal fossils were recovered, that might be skeletal remains of deliberate burials [1]. The site of Regourdou was discovered by chance in 1954 by its owner, Roger Constant [1]. Apart from a Neanderthal skeleton discovered in 1957, excavator Eugène Bonifay found a large number of brown bear bones, several pits and stone platforms that contained bear bones [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
