    ('16f08708-e9ab-4a7e-94b0-2620239d3e34'::uuid, 'category_group', 'Settlements', 'Megalithic', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:16f08708-e9ab-4a7e-94b0-2620239d3e34:category_group', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: category_group ''Megalithic'' restored on Arrephorion', '45ba1c5da54808baba9455405aded025', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "category_group = Settlements from site_type ''Residence/villa/farmhouse'' is in group ''Settlements''"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28048", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0057:chunk-0001: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''Residence/villa/farmhouse''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33149", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0015:chunk-0001: description \"A 5th-century BC building on the northwest edge of the Athenian Acropolis, identified by Wilhelm Dorpfeld in the 1920s as the residence of the Arrephoroi -- two aristocratic girls aged 7-11 chosen annually to serve Athena''s cult. During the nocturnal Arrephoria festival, the girls carried mysterious sealed chests and descended via a secret stairway in the north wall. Only limestone foundations survive; the structure was deliberately reburied in 2006 to protect it for at least 120 years.\" -> ''The Arrephorion or House of the Arrephoroi is a building conjectured to have been on the Acropolis of Athens based on a passage in Pausanias [1]. The discovery of the foundations of a substantial building on the north-west edge of the Acropolis has led to the identification of this structure with the Arrephorion [1]. Plutarch remarks on the existence of a ballcourt adjacent to the house [1]. The physical remains fit what we know of the House of the Arrephoroi but the evidence is still circumstantial that this was in fact the residence of the Arrephoroi [1]. The dimensions of the building are 12.2 m square, and it was erected on a foundation of limestone blocks [1]. The terrace immediately around the building is an artificial one created by infill, which along with the foundation is dated to the last half of the 5th century or contemporary with the Erechtheion [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
