g everything and a central building which she called \"the palace\" [1]. The town itself is centered around the palatial complex which is located on the central-West side of the town [1]. During the Middle Minoan IB period (1925–1875 B.C.E.) substantial construction began which was later destroyed in the Middle Minoan II period (1875–1700 B.C.E.) [1]. Rebuilding occurred in the Middle Minoan III period, which included the palace complex [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('280f2b7d-4978-4352-896d-bcbb03837d3e'::uuid, 'category_group', 'Monuments', 'Settlements', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:280f2b7d-4978-4352-896d-bcbb03837d3e:category_group', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: category_group ''Settlements'' restored on Inti Watana, Ayacucho', '140c36c4b66e652b647e95f838fc21f6', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "category_group = Monuments from site_type ''Archaeological site'' is in group ''Monuments''"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:27901", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0028:chunk-0001: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33461", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0019:chunk-0001: description ''Inca elite retreat and ceremonial complex at 3,126 m elevation beside Lake Pumaqucha (\"Puma Lake\" in Quechua) near Vischongo, Vilcas Huaman Province. The 3,000 m2 complex features an Intihuatana sundial stone used for astronomical observation, a palace built for Inca nobility, a semicircular defensive tower (Torreon), a Sun Gate, and Inca baths with a 13-angled stone still standing after 500+ years. Mortarless stone construction and a hydraulic canal system feeding the lake remain functional to this day. Declared National Cultural Heritage of Peru in 2001.'' -> ''Inti Watana, Intiwatana or Pumaqucha is an archaeological site in Peru [1]. It is located in the Ayacucho Region, Vilcas Huamán Province, Vischongo District, at the lake Pumaqucha [1]. The site was declared a National Cultural Heritage of Peru by Resolución Directoral No. Nº 751/INC on July 27, 2001  [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
