    ('28579aa8-dab5-444d-9ee0-61c95cd1c073'::uuid, 'antiquity', '2', '3', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:28579aa8-dab5-444d-9ee0-61c95cd1c073:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: antiquity ''3'' restored on Viracochapampa', '71d98a4a92146462974211b4f1bed695', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 2 from period_start 601"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28668", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0177:chunk-0001: period_start ''1'' -> ''601''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28669", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0177:chunk-0001: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30368", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35699", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: site_type ''Archaeological site'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44079", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0087:chunk-0001: description ''Viracochapampa (also Huiracochapampa or Wiracochapampa) is an archaeological site in the La Libertad region of Peru, representing one of the administrative centers of the Wari culture [1]. Located approximately 3.5 kilometers north of Huamachuco at an elevation of 3,070 meters, the site contains remains of a building complex of ancient Peru from pre-Inca times [1].'' -> ''Viracochapampa, Huiracochapampa, or Wiracochapampa (possibly from Quechua wiraqucha: mister, sir, gentleman, god; or Wiracocha: one of the greatest Andean divinities; and pampa: plain) is an archaeological site with the remains of a building complex of ancient Peru of pre-Inca times [1]. It was one of the administrative centers of the Wari culture [1]. Viracochapampa is located about 3.5 km north of Huamachuco in the region of La Libertad at an elevation of 3,070 metres [1]. The site was occupied from the late Middle Horizon 1B time to the first decades of period 2A, according to the chronology established by Dorothy Menzel [1]. These correspond to the 7th and 8th centuries of our era [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
