 stone pillaged to build the city wall and other buildings [1]. Today, only the stage area, orchestra section, seating rows, and two columns survive [1]. The Venus of Arles, a famous Roman statue made of marble, was found in pieces at the Roman theatre in 1651 [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
