    ('31c2fc86-3acf-4684-99dc-9f1b35e0f3b4'::uuid, 'category_group', 'Settlements', 'Burial & Death', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:31c2fc86-3acf-4684-99dc-9f1b35e0f3b4:category_group', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: category_group ''Burial & Death'' restored on Santa Rita', '7d541b2422444bfb00f19a9c1500afff', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "category_group = Settlements from site_type ''City/town/settlement'' is in group ''Settlements''"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29728", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0334:chunk-0001: site_type ''Necropolis/tombs complex'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0072:chunk-0001: description ''Santa Rita is a Maya archaeological site on the outskirts of Corozal Town, Belize, believed to be the ancient city of Chetumal. Occupation dates from the Preclassic Period (1200-900 BCE), with burials containing ceramics and shell jewellery from this era. The site survived the Classic Maya collapse and became a major Late Post-Classic trading centre (1350-1530 AD), exchanging jade, obsidian, and gold for locally grown cacao and honey with Northern Yucatan and Highland Guatemala. Excavations by Arlen and Diane Chase (1979-1985) documented its role as capital of the Chetumal Province, one of 19 Maya states recorded by the Spanish. Only Structure 7 remains fully restored, as much of the site was dismantled for modern road fill and building materials.'' -> ''Santa Rita is a Maya ruin and an archaeological reserve on the outskirts of Corozal [1]. Historical evidence suggests that it was probably the ancient and important Maya city known as Chetumal [1]. Evidence excavated at Santa Rita exhibits a long history of inhabitance [1]. Because of its location, the city at Santa Rita once controlled nearby trade routes between the coast and the mouths of two major rivers, the Río Hondo and Río Nuevo [1]. These rivers served as major arteries of trade to centres in the interior such as Lamanai and those in El Petén [1]. Because of this, it became the dominant settlement in the Chetumal region during the early Classic period [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('31c2fc86-3acf-4684-99dc-9f1b35e0f3b4'::uuid, 'fortification', '5', '2', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:31c2fc86-3acf-4684-99dc-9f1b35e0f3b4:fortification', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: fortification ''2'' restored on Santa Rita', '7d541b2422444bfb00f19a9c1500afff', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "fortification = 5 from site_type ''City/town/settlement'' is in group ''Settlements''"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29728", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0334:chunk-0001: site_type ''Necropolis/tombs complex'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0072:chunk-0001: description ''Santa Rita is a Maya archaeological site on the outskirts of Corozal Town, Belize, believed to be the ancient city of Chetumal. Occupation dates from the Preclassic Period (1200-900 BCE), with burials containing ceramics and shell jewellery from this era. The site survived the Classic Maya collapse and became a major Late Post-Classic trading centre (1350-1530 AD), exchanging jade, obsidian, and gold for locally grown cacao and honey with Northern Yucatan and Highland Guatemala. Excavations by Arlen and Diane Chase (1979-1985) documented its role as capital of the Chetumal Province, one of 19 Maya states recorded by the Spanish. Only Structure 7 remains fully restored, as much of the site was dismantled for modern road fill and building materials.'' -> ''Santa Rita is a Maya ruin and an archaeological reserve on the outskirts of Corozal [1]. Historical evidence suggests that it was probably the ancient and important Maya city known as Chetumal [1]. Evidence excavated at Santa Rita exhibits a long history of inhabitance [1]. Because of its location, the city at Santa Rita once controlled nearby trade routes between the coast and the mouths of two major rivers, the Río Hondo and Río Nuevo [1]. These rivers served as major arteries of trade to centres in the interior such as Lamanai and those in El Petén [1]. Because of this, it became the dominant settlement in the Chetumal region during the early Classic period [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
