    ('31ee7df0-cf14-4c97-8d88-697625e5b913'::uuid, 'legacy', '1', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:31ee7df0-cf14-4c97-8d88-697625e5b913:legacy', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: legacy ''4'' restored on Chanquillo', '0442a48ed807cd74e0c9ccacdf495590', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "legacy = 1 from period -500..None, 0 like(s), 0 bookmark(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44119", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0088:chunk-0001: description \"Chankillo is an ancient monumental complex in Peru''s coastal desert, located in the Casma-Sechin basin of Áncash Department. The ruins include a hilltop fort, thirteen stone towers forming a solar observatory dating to the 3rd century BC, and residential and gathering areas [1]. The Thirteen Towers represent one of the oldest known astronomical observatories in the Americas, used to track solar alignments throughout the year [1]. The site was constructed by the Casma/Sechin culture (Sechin Complex) and earned UNESCO World Heritage status in July 2021 [1].\" -> ''Chankillo is an ancient monumental complex in the Peruvian coastal desert, found in the Casma-Sechin basin in the Áncash Department of Peru [1]. The ruins include the hilltop Chankillo fort, the nearby Thirteen Towers solar observatory, and residential and gathering areas [1]. The Thirteen Towers have been interpreted as an astronomical observatory built in the third century BC [1]. The culture that produced Chankillo is called the Casma/Sechin culture or the Sechin Complex [1]. The site covers about four square kilometres and has been interpreted as a fortified temple [1]. The regularly-spaced thirteen towers of Chankillo were constructed atop the ridge of a low hill running near north to south, forming a \"toothed\" horizon with narrow gaps at regular intervals [1]. The Thirteen Towers of Chankillo could be the earliest known observatory in the Americas [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
