    ('349e080c-0b4f-4708-8744-d1b1c6a0b83e'::uuid, 'antiquity', '4', '6', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:349e080c-0b4f-4708-8744-d1b1c6a0b83e:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: antiquity ''6'' restored on Temple of Zeus, Olympia', 'ee196bfed38058fb6ea0c8c09019e084', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 4 from period_start -472"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29690", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0326:chunk-0001: period_start ''-1500'' -> ''-472''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30378", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33587", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0022:chunk-0001: description ''The Temple of Zeus at Olympia, designed by architect Libon of Elis, was built between 470 and 456 BC as the quintessential Doric order Greek temple. It featured six columns across its front, thirteen along each side, and was constructed from local shell-conglomerate covered in white stucco. Inside stood the chryselephantine Statue of Zeus by Phidias, nearly 12 metres tall and counted among the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World. The pediments depicted the chariot race of Pelops and the battle of Lapiths and Centaurs, while metopes illustrated the Twelve Labours of Heracles. Emperor Theodosius II ordered its burning in 426 AD, and earthquakes in 551-552 AD toppled the remains.'' -> ''The Temple of Zeus was an ancient Greek temple in Olympia, Greece, dedicated to the god Zeus [1]. The temple, built in the second quarter of the fifth century BC, was the very model of the fully developed classical Greek temple of the Doric order [1]. The temple was constructed between c.\\u2009472 and 456 BC [1]. The building sat on a crepidoma (platform) of three unequal steps, the exterior columns were positioned in a six by thirteen arrangement, two rows of seven columns divided the cella (inner chamber) into three aisles [1]. The Eastern pediment depicts the chariot race between Pelops and Oenomaus, while the Western pediment features a Centauromachy with Theseus and the Lapiths [1]. The metopes from the temple depict the twelve labours of Heracles [1]. The temple housed the renowned Statue of Zeus, which was one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World [1]. The chryselephantine (gold and ivory) statue was approximately 13 m (43 ft) high, and was made by the sculptor Phidias in his workshop on the site at Olympia [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('349e080c-0b4f-4708-8744-d1b1c6a0b83e'::uuid, 'total_power', '22', '24', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:349e080c-0b4f-4708-8744-d1b1c6a0b83e:total_power', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: total_power ''24'' restored on Temple of Zeus, Olympia', 'ee196bfed38058fb6ea0c8c09019e084', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "total_power = 22 from antiquity + fortification + cultural_influence + mystery + legacy = 4 + 3 + 10 + 4 + 1"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29690", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0326:chunk-0001: period_start ''-1500'' -> ''-472''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30378", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33587", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0022:chunk-0001: description ''The Temple of Zeus at Olympia, designed by architect Libon of Elis, was built between 470 and 456 BC as the quintessential Doric order Greek temple. It featured six columns across its front, thirteen along each side, and was constructed from local shell-conglomerate covered in white stucco. Inside stood the chryselephantine Statue of Zeus by Phidias, nearly 12 metres tall and counted among the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World. The pediments depicted the chariot race of Pelops and the battle of Lapiths and Centaurs, while metopes illustrated the Twelve Labours of Heracles. Emperor Theodosius II ordered its burning in 426 AD, and earthquakes in 551-552 AD toppled the remains.'' -> ''The Temple of Zeus was an ancient Greek temple in Olympia, Greece, dedicated to the god Zeus [1]. The temple, built in the second quarter of the fifth century BC, was the very model of the fully developed classical Greek temple of the Doric order [1]. The temple was constructed between c.\\u2009472 and 456 BC [1]. The building sat on a crepidoma (platform) of three unequal steps, the exterior columns were positioned in a six by thirteen arrangement, two rows of seven columns divided the cella (inner chamber) into three aisles [1]. The Eastern pediment depicts the chariot race between Pelops and Oenomaus, while the Western pediment features a Centauromachy with Theseus and the Lapiths [1]. The metopes from the temple depict the twelve labours of Heracles [1]. The temple housed the renowned Statue of Zeus, which was one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World [1]. The chryselephantine (gold and ivory) statue was approximately 13 m (43 ft) high, and was made by the sculptor Phidias in his workshop on the site at Olympia [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('34c9266e-b55c-4f29-9e6e-eeb547ecfd50'::uuid, 'category_group', 'Fortifications', 'Religious', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:34c9266e-b55c-4f29-9e6e-eeb547ecfd50:category_group', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: category_group ''Religious'' restored on Dun Hallin', '74e160fde5886264922cda163de33a56', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "category_group = Fortifications from site_type ''Fortification'' is in group ''Fortifications''"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28132", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0079:chunk-0001: site_type ''Minaret/tower'' -> ''Fortification''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44123", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0088:chunk-0001: description ''Dun Hallin is an Iron Age Broch located near the northwest coast of the island of Skye, Scotland [1].'' -> ''Dun Hallin is an Iron Age broch located near the northwest coast of the island of Skye, in Scotland [1]. Dun Hallin is located on the Waternish peninsula of Skye, just east of the settlement of Hallin [1]. It occupies the southeast end of a steep-sided rocky plateau overlooking a fertile valley and the sea [1]. Dun Hallin has an external diameter of around 17.4 metres and an internal diameter of around 10.5 metres [1]. The broch walls currently stand to a maximum height of 3.8 metres on the north and west sides [1]. The entrance is on the southeast side but is in a ruined state [1]. On each side of the entrance passage are oval guard cells, although only the northern, right-hand cell can easily be seen [1]. The interior of the broch has much rubble grassed over [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
