e second relief commissioned by Shapur I is situated directly opposite the first [1]. It depicts Shapur I on horseback accompanied by 9 individuals on foot [1]. The latest relief is a bust of the Zoroastrian high priest Kerdir [1]. The relief is dated to the reign of Bahram II, and includes a 31-line inscription in Middle Persian outlining Kerdir\\''s career under the Sasanian monarchs Shapur I, Hormizd I, Bahram I and Bahram II [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
