    ('3f512971-679b-4f40-8f5e-1467424ce605'::uuid, 'legacy', '1', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:3f512971-679b-4f40-8f5e-1467424ce605:legacy', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: legacy ''4'' restored on Dolmen de Viera', 'c204d0b16689bbd33e05339212920f45', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "legacy = 1 from period -4000..None, 0 like(s), 0 bookmark(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33721", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0025:chunk-0001: description ''The Dolmen de Viera is a Copper Age megalithic corridor tomb near Antequera, Malaga, Spain, built c. 3510-3020 BC. Discovered in 1903 by brothers Antonio and Jose Viera, it features a long narrow corridor of 27 orthostatic stones leading to a rectangular burial chamber. Uniquely among the three Antequera dolmens, it faces east so that sunlight reaches the chamber at dawn during the spring and autumn equinoxes. A National Monument since 1923, it was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2016 alongside the Dolmen of Menga and Tholos de El Romeral.'' -> ''The Dolmen de Viera or Dolmen de los Hermanos Viera is a dolmen—a type of single-chamber megalithic tomb—located in Antequera, province of Málaga, Andalusia [1]. It is located only 70 metres from the Dolmen of Menga and about 4 kilometres from Tholos de El Romeral [1]. It was discovered in February 1903 by brothers Antonio and Jose Fuentes from Antequera, who also discovered El Romeral [1]. The Dolmen de Viera was built in the Copper Age, 3510-3020 BC approx. It has had the status of a National monument since 1923 [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
