    ('41701276-d1e1-4068-b767-5b6173f6512c'::uuid, 'category_group', 'Monuments', 'Fortifications', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:41701276-d1e1-4068-b767-5b6173f6512c:category_group', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: category_group ''Fortifications'' restored on Galatas Palace', 'ba3a0cc06b87490bc1a350cc11788435', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "category_group = Monuments from site_type ''Palace'' is in group ''Monuments''"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28935", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0216:chunk-0001: site_type ''Castle/palace'' -> ''Palace''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34365", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0026:chunk-0001: description ''The Galatas Palace is a Minoan archaeological site on Crete, Greece, located about 30 kilometers southeast of Heraklion [1]. Built on an older Protopalatial settlement dating to the MM IB period, a palace was constructed in the early Neopalatial Period during the Early MM IIIA period [1]. The palatial center was destroyed by a conflagration at the end of the MM IIIA period [1]. The site was discovered in the early 1990s [1].'' -> ''The Galatas Palace is a Minoan archaeological site in Heraklion, Crete, Greece about 30 kilometers southeast of the city of Heraklion discovered in the early 1990s [1]. Built on an older Protopalatial settlement dating to the MM IB (c. 1925–1875 BC) period, a Minoan palace was constructed in the early Neopalatial Period, during the Early MM IIIA period (c. 1750 BC) [1]. The east wing is the best-preserved part of the structure, while the West and South wings were found to be extensively damaged [1]. Galatas was discovered in 1992 when illegal excavations revealed the existence of several buildings associated with the Minoans [1]. Excavation of the 4000 square meter palace has unearthed a large, paved central courtyard oriented north and south, that measured 16 meters by 32 meters [1]. The site was occupied beginning in the Early Minoan I (c. 3100–2650 BC) period based on pottery traces [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
