    ('417445b4-e0db-49ac-99db-fe236794e9ff'::uuid, 'legacy', '1', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:417445b4-e0db-49ac-99db-fe236794e9ff:legacy', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: legacy ''4'' restored on Parthenon', '4b3c9972a02d90b15aeaff77a887784f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "legacy = 1 from period -500..None, 0 like(s), 0 bookmark(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:32815", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0009:chunk-0001: description ''The Parthenon, built 447-432 BC on the Athenian Acropolis, is a former temple dedicated to the goddess Athena. Designed by architects Ictinus and Callicrates under the supervision of sculptor Phidias, it used approximately 100,000 tons of Pentelic marble. Over its 2,500-year history it served as a Greek temple, Byzantine church, Catholic cathedral, Ottoman mosque, and ammunition store. A 1687 explosion left it in ruins. A UNESCO World Heritage Site, it remains one of the most iconic symbols of Ancient Greece and Western civilization.'' -> ''The Parthenon is a former temple on the Athenian Acropolis that was dedicated to the goddess Athena [1]. The Parthenon was built in the 5th century BC in thanksgiving for the Greek victory over the Persian invaders during the Greco-Persian Wars [1]. Construction started in 447 BC when the Delian League was at the peak of its power [1]. In the Morean War, a Venetian bomb landed on the Parthenon, which the Ottomans had used as a munitions dump, during the 1687 siege of the Acropolis [1]. The resulting explosion severely damaged the Parthenon [1]. The Parthenon was built under the general supervision of Phidias, who also had charge of the sculptural decoration [1]. The Parthenon is an octastyle peripteral Doric temple with an Ionic hexastyle amphiprostyle two-chambered cella [1]. The cella of the Parthenon housed the chryselephantine statue of Athena Parthenos sculpted by Phidias and dedicated in 439 or 438 BC [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
