 tomb [1]. It was excavated in 1953 by H. E. Kilbride-Jones, aided by Rúaidhrí de Valera and Seán Ó Nualláin, of the Royal Irish Academy [1]. The tomb consists of two chambers which were originally covered by a cairn of stones [1]. The main chamber is 4 metres long and 1.5 metres wide and is formed by a triple-walled gallery [1]. On the northwestern slopes, in a field near the village of Rockbrook, are two standing stones, square in section and approximately 1.8 metres tall [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35754", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: site_type ''Natural feature'' -> ''Necropolis/tombs complex''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('43c12659-d785-44da-ab9b-e0e5fedee349'::uuid, 'category_group', 'Monuments', 'Settlements', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:43c12659-d785-44da-ab9b-e0e5fedee349:category_group', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: category_group ''Settlements'' restored on Molloko', '9b5de18a9b4521555da2a75345c198cd', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "category_group = Monuments from site_type ''Archaeological site'' is in group ''Monuments''"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29378", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0280:chunk-0001: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44325", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0090:chunk-0001: description \"Molloko is an archaeological site in the Puno Region of Peru, about 5 km south of Acora near Lake Titicaca. The site features five fieldstone chullpas (funerary towers) arranged on a hillside, with two quadrangular and two circular plans constructed around one with a square plan. Also known as Kacha Kacha, the site was first documented by Marion Tschopik in 1946 and has been attributed to the Lupaca culture or the Inca period. It was declared a National Cultural Heritage site by Peru''s National Institute of Culture.\" -> ''Molloko (possibly from Aymara for round, round head and swirl) is an archaeological site in Peru [1]. It is located in the Puno Region, Puno Province, Acora District, about 5 km south of the town of Acora, near the village of Molloco [1]. The site was declared a National Cultural Heritage by the National Institute of Culture [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
