    ('45ed713b-bab5-429b-aa62-2f26a08e2a69'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:45ed713b-bab5-429b-aa62-2f26a08e2a69:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: antiquity ''7'' restored on Vryokastro', '6867811f851b2fff447f32af905a557a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1200"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29490", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0295:chunk-0001: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1200''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30389", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34415", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0027:chunk-0001: description ''Vryokastro, on the northwestern coast of Kythnos in the Cyclades, was the ancient capital from which the island takes its name. Inhabited continuously from the 12th century BC to the 7th century AD, the fortified city covered roughly 300 acres with an acropolis, cemeteries, public buildings, and a harbour. Excavations between 2002-2022 uncovered a collapsed Archaic temple yielding approximately 2,000 clay figurines, a sanctuary of Demeter and Kore, and a rare Kythnian silver coin with the head of Apollo. The ancient port at Mandraki Bay has also been explored through underwater archaeology.'' -> \"Vryokastro (Greek: Βρυόκαστρο) is an archaeological site in Kythnos, Greece [1]. It is considered as the ancient capital of the island [1]. It was inhabited from the 12th century BC until the Early Middle Ages [1]. It was called Kythnos in the ancient times and the island was named after it [1]. Vryokastro is on the northwestern side of the island, between the bays of Merichas and Apokrisi [1]. To date, public buildings, an aqueduct, an acropolis, two necropolises, a harbor, a sanctuary, a temple, a monumental mound and a large building of the Classical and Hellenistic period have been found in the settlement''s area [1]. From 2000 to 2016 an excavation of an unplundered sanctuary of the Archaic, Classical and Hellenistic periods was performed [1]. The temple of the sanctuary was intact and contained all the offerings in their place [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
