ed on raised beaches with a southeastern slope [1]. The area elevation ranges between 9 m (30 ft)and 13 m (43 ft) above mean sea level [1]. This part of the island that contains the archaeological site, did not show signs of later occupation by Dorset culture or Thule culture [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
