    ('5e55b918-e5c7-4224-aa90-f244416f696f'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:5e55b918-e5c7-4224-aa90-f244416f696f:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''5'' restored on Pyramid of Hellenikon', 'e35d3d46d648d61be21c76f57a2dc90d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Megalithic stones'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 23 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44427", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0093:chunk-0001: description ''The Pyramid of Hellenikon is an ancient structure in Argolid, Greece [1]. Ancient geographer Pausanias described it as a tomb, while 20th-century researchers have proposed alternative uses [1]. The site is located in the region historically called Apobathmi, which derived its name Pyramia from these pyramid-shaped monuments [1].'' -> ''At the southeastern edge of the plain of Argos, near the springs of river Erasinos and on the main arterial road which during antiquity led from Argos to Tegea and the rest of Arcadia and Kynouria, there is a small structure extant known as the Pyramid of Hellenikon [1]. The pyramid in Hellenikon was excavated first circa 1900 by Theodor Wiegand, who essentially removed all the fill from the floor [1]. The dimensions of the rectangular building surrounding the pyramid of Hellinikon are 7.03 meters by 9.07 metres [1]. The external walls rise at a 60 degree angle up to 3.5 metres [1]. The walls then become vertical in order to support the floor of the building [1]. The entire monument is built from grey limestone from the district in the form of large blocks used in a trapezoidal/partially polygonal system [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
