    ('617627d7-010d-4aa2-a9da-0d3160855f8a'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:617627d7-010d-4aa2-a9da-0d3160855f8a:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''4'' restored on Castell Dinas', '2c030ec8488f56a0c1a5fc16b69b9eb4', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 45 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34627", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0033:chunk-0001: description ''Castell Dinas is a multivallate hillfort and medieval castle in southern Powys, Wales, positioned to defend the Rhiangoll pass between Talgarth and Crickhowell. At 450 m elevation, it holds the highest castle in England and Wales. The hillfort dates to the Iron Age (c. 800 BC - AD 74) and is roughly oval, covering about 9 hectares. A Norman stone castle was built within it around 1070-1075, possibly by William Fitz Osbern, though standing remains date to the 13th century. The castle was captured and destroyed by Llywelyn ap Gruffudd in 1265 and never rebuilt.'' -> ''Castell Dinas is a hillfort and castle in southern Powys, Wales [1]. At 450 m it has the highest castle in England and Wales [1]. It is positioned to defend the Rhiangoll pass between Talgarth and Crickhowell [1]. A fortified Norman castle with stone walls was built on the site possibly by William Fitz Osbern or his son Roger de Breteuil, Earl of Hereford in the period 1070 to 1075 [1]. The fortress seems to have been constructed in stone from the first with a hall-keep surrounded with curtain walls and square towers [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
