    ('62f21f04-c668-474e-8548-69bbdbc35620'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:62f21f04-c668-474e-8548-69bbdbc35620:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''5'' restored on Megarian Treasury, Olympia', 'fbbacc40c05bb371e0a870bfd23e6aba', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Megalithic structures'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 21 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34639", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0033:chunk-0001: description ''The Megarian Treasury at Olympia, dating to c. 520-510 BC, was built by the city-state of Megara on the north side of the sanctuary to store votive offerings. Constructed primarily of limestone with a terracotta tile roof, it featured a pediment depicting a Gigantomachy (battle between gods and giants) carved in limestone relief. The restored entablature and pediment sculpture, with one giant figure surviving nearly intact, are now displayed in the Olympia Archaeological Museum.'' -> ''The Megarian Treasury at Olympia, was an ancient Greek building, located in the sanctuary of Olympia, which held votive offerings of the Greek city-state of Megara [1]. The Megarian Treasury was mainly built from limestone, with the roof made of terracotta tiles [1]. The building was adorned with several statues, including limestone reliefs and carvings in cedarwood [1]. Due to its architectural styling, both the statues and the building itself are believed by archaeologists to originate from the 500s BCE [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
