theatre was built at the foot of the La Croix-Rousse hill at what was then the confluence of the Rhône and Saône  [1]. An inscription on one of the blocks found in 1957 connects the amphitheatre with the sanctuary of Rome and Augustus and allows its origins to be identified [1]. The amphitheatre was expanded at the start of the 2nd century, according to J. Guey by C. Julius Celse [1]. The first excavations between 1818 and 1820 revealed the perimeter of the arena before re-covering it [1]. From 1956 serious excavations were begun, followed by 1966/67, 1971/72 and 1976/78 campaigns [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
