    ('6c2319ca-2998-4408-a7d8-2939397c300e'::uuid, 'antiquity', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:6c2319ca-2998-4408-a7d8-2939397c300e:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: antiquity ''8'' restored on Myrtos Pyrgos', 'eb71e609069d5b4de47efa94d313970a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 7 from period_start -3000"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28584", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0164:chunk-0001: period_start ''-4500'' -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30429", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44485", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0095:chunk-0001: description ''Pyrgos (also Myrtos-Pyrgos) is a Minoan archaeological site near Myrtos in the municipality of Ierapetra on the south coast of Crete. The site provides evidence of settlements along the southern Ierapetra Isthmus [1]. It is located close to the Myrtos valley and features a harbor with a nearby mountain range providing natural protection [1]. The settlement includes a courtyard, multiple rooms, a country house, and a tomb [1].'' -> ''Pyrgos (also Myrtos-Pyrgos; Greek: Πύργος [στο Μύρτος]) is an archaeological site of the Minoan civilization near Myrtos in the municipality of Ierapetra on the south coast of Crete [1]. Pyrgos provides evidence of settlements along the southern Ierapetra Isthmus [1]. The settlement includes a courtyard, many rooms, a country house and a tomb [1]. In 1970 the site began to be excavated by archaeologist Gerald Cadogan [1]. Myrtos Pyrgos is used as an example of what an administrative site during the Minoan civilization looks like [1]. The country house was built in the Late Minoan Period and was built atop of a hill [1]. Inside the tomb, archaeologists found clay vases and cups [1]. In addition, knives, daggers, and triton shells were also found [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
