e site began to be excavated by archaeologist Gerald Cadogan [1]. Myrtos Pyrgos is used as an example of what an administrative site during the Minoan civilization looks like [1]. The country house was built in the Late Minoan Period and was built atop of a hill [1]. Inside the tomb, archaeologists found clay vases and cups [1]. In addition, knives, daggers, and triton shells were also found [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
