ously, they had been built out of wood [1]. The amphitheatre was designed to host around 20,000 people [1]. One of the most notable events in the amphitheatre''s history occurred around 59 AD, when a deadly brawl occurred between Pompeiians and residents of Nuceria during games in the amphitheatre, resulting in a 10-year ban on such events there [1]. The amphitheatre was damaged by an earthquake in 62 AD [1]. The amphitheatre was first partially excavated in 1748 [1]. It was later completely excavated between 1813 and 1816 [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
