ks of local hard volcanic rock (rhyodacite) [1]. Nine blocks still stand and three are now fallen [1]. The site was discovered and excavated by Georgi Nehrizov in around 1998–1999 [1]. The excavations uncovered decorated pottery, as well as bronze artefacts (a fibula and a pin) [1]. These date the construction of the cromlech to the second phase of the Early Iron Age (8th–6th centuries BC) [1]. The site continued in use into the late Iron Age [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35857", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-800'' -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('82b9ba8e-bc9a-405a-afe2-fcb210a5d278'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '7', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:82b9ba8e-bc9a-405a-afe2-fcb210a5d278:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''7'' restored on Llamachayuq', '117f671d052a7eaa81ee812904afa569', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Petroglyphs'', ''1000 - 1500 AD'') is shared by 5 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44735", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0098:chunk-0001: description \"Llamachayuq is an archaeological complex featuring petroglyphs in Peru''s Apurimac Region [1]. The site contains rock carvings depicting llamas, vicunas, felines, human figures, and the sun [1]. Located at 3,449 meters elevation near Lliupapuquio in the San Jeronimo District, the rock art represents a significant example of Andean artistic traditions [1].\" -> ''Llamachayuq (Quechua llama llama, -cha, -yuq suffixes, \"with a little llama (or llamas)\", also spelled Llamachayoq) is an archaeological complex with petroglyphs in Peru [1]. It is located in the Apurímac Region, Andahuaylas Province, San Jerónimo District [1]. The site with images of llamas, vicuñas, felines, people and the sun lies near Lliwpa Pukyu (Lliupapuquio) at a height of 3,449 metres (11,316 ft) [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
