    ('83893760-fcb6-4824-8ee9-7e1c6fc74852'::uuid, 'mystery', '9', '8', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:83893760-fcb6-4824-8ee9-7e1c6fc74852:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''8'' restored on Dead Woman''s Ditch', '7ff204a5d973343f7b01ceaa8039e861', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 9 from (''Earthwork'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 2 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35097", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0041:chunk-0001: description \"Dead Woman''s Ditch is a prehistoric linear earthwork in Over Stowey, Somerset, England, on the Quantock Hills [1]. It consists of a bank with a ditch along the west side, running approximately 950 metres (3,120 ft) from Lady''s Fountain spring across Robin Uprights Hill into Ramscombe. Scheduled as an ancient monument, its origin predates 4500 BC, but its purpose remains unknown, though it has been linked to the nearby hillfort at Dowsborough.\" -> \"Dead Woman''s Ditch is an earthwork which has been scheduled as an ancient monument in Over Stowey, Somerset, England situated on the Quantock Hills [1]. The earthwork is presumed to be of prehistoric origin and is of unknown purpose, but has been linked to Dowsborough [1]. The 1 kilometre long earthwork has been cut through by later tracks and a road [1]. It is badly eroded in places and is on the Heritage at Risk Register [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
