    ('88897642-cf8a-48c2-a9a4-ebb0408a8804'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:88897642-cf8a-48c2-a9a4-ebb0408a8804:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''6'' restored on Innisidgen', '66fd043490fbed90d04fa1fe9461a9ef', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Cemetery'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 10 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44769", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0099:chunk-0001: description ''Innisidgen is the site of two Bronze Age entrance graves (c. 2500-800 BC) on Innisidgen Hill, St Mary\\''s, Isles of Scilly, overlooking Crow Sound toward the Eastern Isles. Upper Innisidgen, also known as \"The Giant\\''s Grave,\" is one of the best-preserved entrance graves on Scilly, with a mound measuring 30 by 26 feet and a chamber roofed by five massive capstones. Lower Innisidgen, located 300 feet northwest, is more damaged and retains only two capstones. Entrance graves are a burial type unique to Scilly and West Cornwall. Both chambers were found empty when first entered in modern times, though such graves typically contained cremated bone and funerary urns. A prehistoric field system survives on the adjoining slope.'' -> ''Innisidgen is the site of two Bronze Age entrance graves on the island of St Mary\\''s in the Isles of Scilly [1]. The two burial monuments, (Upper and Lower Innisidgen) lie on a steep slope of Innisidgen Hill overlooking Crow Sound with a view towards the Eastern Isles [1]. Innisidgen Hill is a scheduled monument on the Isles of Scilly, north east of Hugh Town [1]. Lower Innisidgen lies near the bottom of the northern slope of Innisidgen Hill [1]. This grave is more damaged than the upper grave and has only two of its original capstones [1]. Upper Innisidgen, also known as \"The Giant\\''s Grave\", is one of the best preserved entrance graves on Scilly [1]. The entrance grave consists of a slightly oblong mound of earth and rubble measuring 9m by 8m, and is 1.8m in height [1]. The mound covers an intact burial chamber with an entrance at the eastern side of the mound [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
