    ('8a30c67b-4f3e-4e14-b249-bf7de6d7ff31'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '5', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:8a30c67b-4f3e-4e14-b249-bf7de6d7ff31:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''5'' restored on Tomb of Clytemnestra', '61555f0081d99c0a11ed61be88a80a93', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Tomb'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 6 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28372", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0120:chunk-0001: period_start ''-1500'' -> ''-1250''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28374", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0120:chunk-0002: site_type ''Necropolis/tombs complex'' -> ''Tomb''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35871", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-1250'' -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:36799", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0043:chunk-0001: description ''The Tomb of Clytemnestra is a Mycenaean tholos (beehive) tomb constructed around 1250 BC in the Argolid region of Greece[1]. Its monumental façade features carved stone lintels and semi-columns that influenced later Greek and Roman architecture[1]. Alongside the Treasury of Atreus, it ranks as one of the most impressive examples of Mycenaean funerary architecture from the Late Bronze Age[1]. The tomb is named after Clytemnestra, wife of legendary King Agamemnon, though archaeological evidence does not confirm a specific royal burial[1].'' -> ''The Tomb of Clytemnestra is a Mycenaean tholos type tomb built in c. 1250 BC [1]. The Tomb of Clytemnestra with its imposing façade is together with the Treasury of Atreus the most monumental tomb of that type [1]. The entrance to the tomb consists of a dromos with walls of ashlar in conglomerate [1]. The exterior façade of the stomion is decorated with half-columns made of gypsum which were carefully carved with ornate capitals and vertical fluting [1]. A large relieving triangle overlaps the door lintel [1]. It was originally decorated by a colored relief sculpture [1]. Through the lintel block a small drain is cut in the rock, lined with low rubble walls and roofed with small slabs [1]. During the Ottoman rule of Greece the tomb was raided by Veli Pasha [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
