    ('8d416cb3-e799-4990-96a9-50a70fde39c2'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:8d416cb3-e799-4990-96a9-50a70fde39c2:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''4'' restored on Moel y Gest', '57f9aea53101738eeee77f4c69beeb1e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 45 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:36829", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0044:chunk-0001: description \"Moel y Gest is a Bronze Age hillfort on a 263m Marilyn in North Wales, dating to 3000–1500 BC[1][2]. The rocky summit''s high prominence and far-reaching views of Snowdon, the Llŷn Peninsula, and Rhinogydd made it a strategic defensive location[1].\" -> ''Moel y Gest is a 263 m hill to the west of Porthmadog in North Wales [1]. At the summit of Moel y Gest is a hillfort which shows some resemblance to the \"nuclear forts\" of the Early Middle Ages found in Scotland [1]. Like these, it has a \"court\" system with loops of wall and a \"citadel\" [1]. For most of its perimeter, the boundary defenses follow natural features to give it good defensive potential, but at the northwestern part, where the entrance lies, it is set back from the cliff making it vulnerable to an approaching enemy who would be invisible until close at hand [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
