site probably contemporary with the church, stand within the hillfort on the north-eastern side [1]. The site is a Scheduled Ancient Monument [3].\" -> \"Caerau Hillfort is a large triangular multivallate Iron Age hillfort, built on a previously occupied Neolithic site, occupying the western tip of an extensive ridge-top plateau in the western suburbs of Caerau and Ely, Cardiff, Wales [1]. Excavations for an episode of Channel 4''s Time Team showed the hillfort''s occupation began about 600 BC [1]. Further excavations, in 2013–2014, revealed evidence of the site''s occupation back to the early Neolithic [1]. Finds included flint tools and weapons dating to 3600 BC [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
    ('936b5a30-e1dd-4524-95c2-e7214ecf3090'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:936b5a30-e1dd-4524-95c2-e7214ecf3090:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''4'' restored on Archaeological Site of Grand', 'c2994dc4a469e15dfdc7bd651b6cc32f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Megalithic structures'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 22 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44823", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0100:chunk-0001: description \"Gallo-Roman sanctuary of Apollo Grannus, the healing god, in the Vosges department of northeastern France, identified with Andesina on the Peutinger Table. Its 1st-century amphitheatre seated 17,000 spectators, making it one of the largest in the Roman Empire. A 232-square-metre floor mosaic from an ancient basilica depicts four wild animals around a central theatrical scene from Menander''s Phasma. The town was enclosed by a rampart and developed as a major pilgrimage centre for healing rituals dedicated to Apollo Grannus.\" -> ''The archaeological site of Grand contains a wide amphitheater and a mosaic of 232 m2 [1]. It is located in the French department of Vosges, in the region Grand Est, in France [1]. It was an ancient Gallo-Roman city named Andésina (15,000-20,000 inhabitants) [1]. The amphitheater was built at the end of the 1st century and can contain 17,000 people [1]. At its center, the mosaic shows a theater scene of the Phasma of Menander and four animals at the four corners [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
