on as he concluded that the site was a burial mound, excavations were terminated [1]. In the 1930s, the site was investigated by a team of scholars from Melitopol under Valentin Danylenko [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('944099e9-5dfb-435f-a1a2-0c87eb4660be'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:944099e9-5dfb-435f-a1a2-0c87eb4660be:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''4'' restored on Troldkirken', 'ae82030c657db2bcc31d2a60f61baac6', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Necropolis/tombs complex'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 47 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44827", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0100:chunk-0001: description ''Troldkirken (\"Church of the Troll\") is a Neolithic long barrow near Nibe, Denmark, constructed by the Funnelbeaker culture around 3500 BC. The monument stretches nearly 50 metres long and 12 metres wide, encircled by 47 large megaliths with a polygonal dolmen chamber topped by a capstone weighing approximately 7,000 kilograms. It became a protected site in 1809, making it one of the first prehistoric monuments officially preserved by the Danish government. The site offers panoramic views over the Limfjorden.'' -> ''Troldkirken is a Stone Age long barrow in the village of Nibe, Denmark [1]. The barrow was constructed by the Funnelbeaker culture around 3500 BC and is marked out by 47 megaliths [1]. Placed on the top of the barrow is a polygonal chambered dolmen with a large capstone [1]. The whole monument is some 50 metres long [1]. The name \"Troldkirken\" means both Church of the Troll and Church of Sorcery in Danish [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
