    ('98c794a6-57b5-4783-b38d-3693bb60b91b'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:98c794a6-57b5-4783-b38d-3693bb60b91b:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''5'' restored on Athenian Treasury, Delphi', 'b1e65ce23d5478159c09fe896219969f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Megalithic structures'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 21 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43591", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0077:chunk-0001: description ''Small Doric treasury built entirely of Parian marble along the Sacred Way at Delphi, Greece, dating to circa 490 BC. Traditionally attributed to spoils from the Battle of Marathon, its inscription reads \"The Athenians to Apollo from the Medes\". Thirty metopes depict the labours of Theseus and Heracles, representing the earliest large-scale sculptural depiction of Theseus. Reconstructed by French archaeologists in 1903-1906 using four-fifths of the original stone; the metopes on-site are replicas, with originals in the Delphi Museum.'' -> ''The Athenian Treasury at Delphi was constructed by the Athenians to house dedications and votive offerings made by their city and citizens to the sanctuary of Apollo [1]. The entire treasury, including its sculptural decoration, is built of Parian marble [1]. The date of construction is disputed, and scholarly opinions range from 510 to 480 BCE [1]. The Athenian treasury metopes display the earliest known presence of Theseus in a large-scale sculpture [1]. The building was excavated by the French School at Athens, led by Pierre de La Coste-Messelière, and reconstructed from 1903 to 1906 [1]. The thirty metopes of the treasury are 67 cm tall and 62–64 cm wide depicting the labors of Theseus and Herakles [1]. The Athenian Treasury in Delphi was built according to a typical distyle in antis design, with two antae framing two columns [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
