    ('9e4cc13d-57c5-484f-9a55-8770ac95019a'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:9e4cc13d-57c5-484f-9a55-8770ac95019a:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''4'' restored on Sanctuary of Pandion', '18b5abc5028c65d7f2c81983b5efe98a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Sanctuary'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 6 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28110", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0074:chunk-0001: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''Sanctuary''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:36987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0048:chunk-0001: description ''The Sanctuary of Pandion is an open-air walled sanctuary in the southeast corner of the Acropolis of Athens, measuring 40 by 17.5 metres, built around 450 BC during the Periclean building program. The rectangular structure was divided into two nearly equal sections by a wall, with a projecting portico on the western side. It is identified as the heroon (hero shrine) of Pandion, the eponymous hero of the Attic tribe Pandionis. The 2nd-century AD traveller Pausanias recorded visiting the sanctuary and seeing a statue of Pandion there. Its foundations were unearthed during excavations for the Acropolis museum construction.'' -> ''The Sanctuary of Pandion was an ancient Greek sanctuary on the Acropolis of Athens [1]. It is known from ancient inscriptions and from the writings of the traveller Pausanias to have been located on the eastern side of the Acropolis, and to have contained a statue of the hero Pandion, to whom it was dedicated [1]. In antiquity, the Sanctuary of Pandion was the heroon of Pandion, the eponymous hero of the Attic tribe Pandionis [1]. The Sanctuary of Pandion is usually identified with a building in the southeast corner of the Acropolis [1]. This building was excavated in a campaign begun in 1885 by Panagiotis Kavvadias in collaboration with the German architect Georg Kawerau [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
