    ('9ed175c7-a706-4a71-b10a-f93a68734afc'::uuid, 'mystery', '10', '9', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:9ed175c7-a706-4a71-b10a-f93a68734afc:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''9'' restored on The Gop', 'e2a7c968b6269ab37180a78315bbc74e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 10 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 1 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:32725", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0001:chunk-0001: description ''A massive Neolithic cairn on Gop Hill in Flintshire, Wales, and the second-largest ancient human-made mound in Britain after Silbury Hill. The oval monument stands 14 m high with a maximum diameter of 101 m, constructed of limestone blocks with drystone walling. Boyd Dawkins excavated in 1886-87 using tunnels and a shaft but found no burial chamber, leaving its function uncertain. The Gop Cave beneath yielded fourteen human skeletons, a stone axe, and Peterborough pottery indicating Neolithic activity. Whether it served as a passage grave, ceremonial platform, or hillfort remains debated.'' -> ''The Gop (Welsh: Coparleni, also known as Gop Cairn or Gop-y-Goleuni) is a Neolithic monument lying within the Clwydian Range, northwest of Trelawnyd, in Flintshire, Wales [1]. Sitting on top of Gop Hill, a natural outcrop of Carboniferous Limestone, the cairn mound is 75-80m in diameter and 12m high [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
