    ('a023ea22-2689-4ec1-9b56-6b6f7ed023b0'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:a023ea22-2689-4ec1-9b56-6b6f7ed023b0:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''7'' restored on Dolmen of Pedra Branca', 'baa56695381c30627debdc7e2d9ac8ad', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Dolmen'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 16 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:36997", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0048:chunk-0001: description ''The Dolmen of Pedra Branca is a Late Neolithic and Chalcolithic burial tomb in Vale de Figueira, parish of Melides, Grandola municipality, Setubal District, Portugal. Built c. 2500 BC and reused around 2000 BC, it features a polygonal main chamber (3.85 x 3.4 m) with 7 pillars and a trapeze-shaped gallery with 5 pillars, reached by an entrance corridor. The chamber roof was supported by a 2.20 m tall quartzite pillar. Excavations uncovered approximately 65 skeletal remains alongside slate plaque necklaces and stone tools. The site is classified as a Public Interest Construction.'' -> \"The Dolmen of Pedra Branca is a burial tomb, used in the late Neolithic and, subsequently, in the late Chalcolithic periods [1]. It is situated in the Vale de Figueira in the parish of Melides, which is in the Grândola municipality of Setubal [1]. The burial chamber''s roof (in stone or wooden slabs) was supported in the middle by a large, 2.2 meter tall, quartzite pillar, which had the structural function of sharing the weight of the crypt''s roof with the other supports [1]. The main polygonal chamber, measuring 3.85 m x 3.4 m, reached by an entrance corridor, was covered by transverse slabs [1]. A trapezoidal chamber on the left side was a separate compartment, measuring 3.5m x 1.5m [1]. In addition to skeletons, many funerary offerings have been discovered [1]. The dolmen is situated high on a hill that visually dominates the surrounding Vale de Figueira area [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
