    ('ab699722-9c7e-464a-b507-74a21078411c'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '3', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:ab699722-9c7e-464a-b507-74a21078411c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''3'' restored on Watling Temple', 'c1e6d63ccc42bd412e61f8eb6cb70b66', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Temple'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 10 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28477", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0141:chunk-0001: period_start ''1'' -> ''-30''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28478", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0141:chunk-0001: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''Temple''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30479", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35938", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35939", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-30'' -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43643", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0078:chunk-0001: description ''Romano-Celtic temple discovered in 2019 within a Roman industrial town near the A2 road at Newington, Kent. The square flint-walled temple measured 12.5m by 11.5m and is one of only 150 recorded temples in England. Excavation of the 7.2-hectare site also revealed iron furnaces, pottery kilns, a 7m-wide Roman road, and late Iron Age remains dating from 30 BC. A full-scale reconstruction was unveiled in 2021, positioned 70m from the original location.'' -> ''Watling Temple is the name given to the remains of a temple within a Roman town next to the modern A2 road in Newington, near Sittingbourne in Kent, England [1]. The town was rediscovered in 2019 during an archaeological dig covering 18 acres that found iron furnaces and pottery kilns as part of a manufacturing site, a Roman temple, a 7 metres wide Roman road and late Iron Age remains dating from 30 BC [1]. The Roman road Watling Street runs through the village of Newington, and the newly discovered road predates it and takes an alternative route [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
