    ('b4666064-903d-4db2-a282-38897ac4c1a1'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:b4666064-903d-4db2-a282-38897ac4c1a1:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''6'' restored on Dun Fiadhairt Broch', '081df875d50a5852405fccd413d7b7c7', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Minaret/tower'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 9 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44963", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0104:chunk-0001: description ''Dun Fiadhairt is an Iron Age broch located on the north coast of the island of Skye, Scotland [1].'' -> ''Dun Fiadhairt is an Iron Age broch located on the north coast of the island of Skye [1]. The broch stands on a low, rocky knoll, in the midst of moorland, on a peninsula which juts into the east side of Loch Dunvegan [1]. The broch has an external diameter of 16.8 metres and an internal diameter of 9.6 metres [1]. Dun Fiadhairt was excavated around 1892 by the Countess Vincent Baillet de Latour [1]. Finds included a quantity of pottery, and a large amount of \"iron refuse\" [1]. Stone finds included a rotary quern, a whetstone, a hammerstone, spindle whorls and a fragment of an armlet [1]. Several glass beads were found of various colours, and in addition there were 59 amber beads in the form of short cylinders which presumably formed a necklace [1]. There was also found a baked clay object, thought to be a Roman votive model of a bale of wool [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
