e Late Archaic, Classical, Hellenistic, and Early Roman periods [1]. There are also recorded archaeological finds from the Late Roman and early medieval periods [1]. Palagruža consists of one larger island, called Vela or Velika Palagruža, and a smaller one, Mala Palagruža, as well as a dozen nearby rocks and reefs composed of dolomite [1]. The archipelago is 123 km south of Split on the Croatian mainland, 60 km south-west of Lastovo, Croatia, and 53 km north-north-east of the Gargano peninsula in Italy [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('be92ce6c-0c0e-43da-b5b8-be9137f0e151'::uuid, 'category_group', 'Monuments', 'Settlements', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:be92ce6c-0c0e-43da-b5b8-be9137f0e151:category_group', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: category_group ''Settlements'' restored on Pachat''aqa', '6b43353ab64eabc97e3d762dc670eb08', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "category_group = Monuments from site_type ''Archaeological site'' is in group ''Monuments''"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29476", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0292:chunk-0001: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1764''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29477", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0292:chunk-0001: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35977", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-1764'' -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:37429", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0055:chunk-0001: description ''Pachat\\''aqa, also known as the Inca\\''s Gallows, is a pre-Inca astronomical observatory located approximately 600 metres south of Copacabana, Bolivia, near Lake Titicaca. The site consists of two parallel stone blocks forming a lintel structure atop Kesanani hill, used to determine seasons, track lunar movements, and predict eclipses. Dating to approximately 1764 BC during the Chiripa culture period, its name derives from Aymara meaning \"place where time is measured\". The Cosmic Physics Institute of Bolivia has confirmed the site\\''s astronomical alignment capabilities.'' -> \"Pachataka (also spelled Pachataca or Pachat''aqa), commonly known as the Inca Gallows, is an archaeological site in Bolivia, located near Lake Titicaca in the municipality of Copacabana, Manco Kapac Province [1]. Pachataka is a pre-Inca astronomical observatory formed by a lintel made of two parallel stone blocks [1]. It was used to determine the seasons, track lunar movements, and predict eclipses [1]. It is located at the summit of Mount Kesanani, approximately 600 meters south of the town of Copacabana [1]. According to mathematical and astronomical calculations conducted by the Institute of Cosmic Physics of Bolivia, the observatory dates approximately to 1764 B.C., during the era of the Chiripa culture [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
