    ('c30712db-a675-4203-a442-cb3f9b1c5848'::uuid, 'civilization', 'Georgia', 'Georgia (country)', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:c30712db-a675-4203-a442-cb3f9b1c5848:civilization', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: civilization ''Georgia (country)'' restored on Tsona Cave', '8cea1d09fd3c0af861e37617990f6419', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "civilization = Georgia from country ''Georgia''"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:27271", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-21_mechanical-country: country ''Georgia (country)'' -> ''Georgia''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:37469", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0056:chunk-0001: description ''Tsona Cave is an archaeological cave site at the head of the river Qvirila near village Tson in Java Municipality, Shida Kartli, Georgia[1]. Dated to the period between 500 BC and 1 AD, the cave contains archaeological evidence of ancient human occupation in this high-altitude mountain environment[2].'' -> ''Tsona Cave is an archaeological site at the head of the river Qvirila in proximity of village Tson in the Java Municipality in Shida Kartli in Georgia [1]. The site is close to the Bouba-Kakheri pass at south of the Caucasus range [1]. Tsona Cave was discovered by A. Kalandadze in 1958 [1]. It was excavated by Kalandadze, Tushabramishvili and later by Z. Kikodze [1]. The cave is located at 2100 m above sea level and therefore it is one of the highest archaeological cave sites in the country [1]. Excavations at the site revealed Lower and Middle Paleolithic archaeological remains [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
