    ('c75b6409-59b2-4675-a402-796d4b2ba6fb'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:c75b6409-59b2-4675-a402-796d4b2ba6fb:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''4'' restored on Kilclooney More', 'f20cf15f6bbee197dad45643a5e3ffe6', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Megalithic structures'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 18 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:27794", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0010:chunk-0001: site_type ''Megalithic stones'' -> ''Megalithic structures''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:37507", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0057:chunk-0001: description ''A Neolithic megalithic complex in County Donegal, Ireland, featuring two portal tombs built into a 26-metre-long trapezoidal mound, dating to c. 4000-3000 BC. The larger northeastern tomb has portal stones 1.8 m high and a dramatic capstone 4.2 m long, while the smaller southwestern chamber measures 1.5 m long and 1 m wide. Excavation recovered Neolithic pottery sherds of the Lyles Hill tradition (c. 3800-3500 BC), now held by the National Museum of Ireland. The site lies on the Loughrea Peninsula between Narin and Ardara.'' -> ''Kilclooney More belongs to the low-lying land in the west of County Donegal that is prominent for its concentration of court and portal tombs [1]. In the Neolithic period this land was fertile due to a warmer and drier climate, supporting farming communities who crafted ceramics and built tombs which are still described as ‘magnificent’ [1]. The smaller portal tomb of Kilclooney More is located west of the R261, in a shallow basin north of the Abberachrin River [1]. The eastern portal stone is missing but otherwise the tomb is well preserved [1]. The chamber is comparatively small, measuring 1.45 m × 1.2 m, pointed in SSE direction [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
