    ('c9358837-e3ee-4daa-aedc-34e45afa1692'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:c9358837-e3ee-4daa-aedc-34e45afa1692:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''7'' restored on Combs Ditch', 'c8f01e7bb69df115cb5ad35c20313fd3', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Earthwork'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 11 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:32809", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0007:chunk-0001: description ''Combs Ditch is a linear earthwork on Charlton Down in Dorset, England [1]. The earthwork serves as a parish boundary, separating Charlton Marshall and Spetisbury to the north-east from Winterborne Whitechurch, Winterborne Kingston and Anderson to the south-west [1]. Combs Ditch is a scheduled ancient monument [1].'' -> \"Combs Ditch (sometimes spelt Comb''s Ditch or Combe Ditch) is a linear earthwork on Charlton Down in Dorset, England [1]. The earthwork is a scheduled ancient monument [1]. The earthwork consists of a bank with a ditch on the north east side [1]. It was once at least 6.4 kilometres long but now only 4.4 kilometres is visible [1]. The bank ranges from 5.4 to 8.5 metres wide with a maximum height of 2.2 metres [1]. The ditch varies in width from 4.8 to 8.5 metres [1]. Excavation found third- or fourth-century Roman pottery lying on the turf line behind the bank probably before its final reconstruction [1]. The limited excavation seems to show an Iron Age boundary ditch being enlarged into a defensive earthwork in the late Roman or post-Roman period [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
