1]. The major axis of the structure is 170 metres and the minor axis is 139 metres [1]. The façade had a total height of 46 metres, divided into four levels, all of the Tuscan order [1]. The lower three levels consisted of 80 arches, each made of travertine and decorated with a bust of a god in the keystone [1]. The structure was used as a fortress by the Lombard princes of Capua [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
