    ('cf82ed54-d7e1-4a86-9b24-2abfdb6ff881'::uuid, 'category_group', 'Infrastructure', 'Megalithic', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:cf82ed54-d7e1-4a86-9b24-2abfdb6ff881:category_group', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: category_group ''Megalithic'' restored on Cornalvo Dam', '84abd8c9f012ca5b682f886ff105306e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "category_group = Infrastructure from site_type ''Reservoir/aqueduct/canal'' is in group ''Infrastructure''"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28097", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0071:chunk-0001: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''Reservoir/aqueduct/canal''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:45281", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0108:chunk-0001: description ''The Cornalvo Dam is a Roman gravity dam built in the 1st-2nd century AD to supply water to Augusta Emerita (modern Merida), capital of Lusitania province. Standing approximately 24 m high and 200 m long, it blocks the Albarregas River with an earth fill core faced with dressed ashlar and Roman concrete. Remarkably, the dam remains in use today, impounding a horn-shaped reservoir about 4 km long. Declared a National Monument in 1912, it forms part of the Archaeological Ensemble of Merida, a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1993.'' -> ''The Cornalvo Dam is a Roman gravity dam built to supply water to the Roman colonia of Emerita Augusta, capital of the Roman province of Lusitania [1]. It was built in the 1st–2nd century AD as part of the infrastructure which supplied water [1]. The dam is part of the Archaeological Ensemble of Mérida, which is one of the largest and most extensive archaeological sites in Spain and that was declared a World Heritage Site by UNESCO in 1993 [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
