    ('d799bb0f-8ffd-4a29-a516-ffd445f6b699'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:d799bb0f-8ffd-4a29-a516-ffd445f6b699:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''8'' restored on Overstone Anglo-Saxon Cemetery', 'cf13a9b0a6cda7508892b2fc2f53f755', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Cemetery'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 7 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:32729", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0001:chunk-0001: description ''Anglo-Saxon burial site discovered in 2019 near Overstone, Northamptonshire, England. The 15 hectare cemetery is the largest Anglo-Saxon burial ground found in Northamptonshire [1]. Excavation by the Museum of London Archaeology yielded 154 graves containing 3,000 artefacts [1].'' -> ''Overstone Anglo-Saxon cemetery is an Anglo-Saxon place of burial discovered at the Overstone Leys housing development site near the village of Overstone, Northamptonshire [1]. The burial site was found during an archaeological investigation in 2019 [1]. It is the biggest Anglo-Saxon cemetery ever found in Northamptonshire [1]. The 15 hectare site was excavated in 2019 by the Museum of London Archaeology over a 12 month period [1]. Uncovered during the excavation were 154 individual graves and 3000 artefacts [1]. Included in the individual burials were many grave goods, consisting primarily of jewellery and weapons [1]. A group of 22 previously unknown Anglo-Saxon era structures were also found at the site [1]. The assemblage was a combination of sunken-feature buildings and post-built structures [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
