    ('d7cecc1a-ed47-4dd6-a335-69e1233d47aa'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:d7cecc1a-ed47-4dd6-a335-69e1233d47aa:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''7'' restored on Roman Baths of Toledo', '1906d6d45123c9c88dd63952f3fd1d31', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Bath'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 15 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:45311", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0109:chunk-0001: description ''(Late 1st–mid-2nd c. AD) The Roman Baths of Toledo, also known as the Roman Thermae of Amador de los Ríos, are ruins of Roman thermae located in Toledo, Castile-La Mancha, Spain [1]. The baths were part of the urban water supply system for the Roman city of Toletum, serving to provide clean water to residents [1]. Based on the scale of surviving infrastructure, the facility is believed to have been a public bath complex rather than private [1].'' -> \"The Roman baths of Toledo or Roman thermae of Amador de los Ríos are ruins of Roman thermae located in the city of Toledo in Castile-La Mancha, Spain [1]. The baths can be seen as part of the system of supplying clean water to the city (then known by the Latin name of Toletum) [1]. From the scale of the surviving infrastructure, they are assumed to have been a public facility [1]. As regards chronology, the remains correspond to a period between the end of the 1st century and mid-2nd century CE [1]. The location of the baths at Amador de los Ríos square is high above the River Tagus [1]. In Roman times water was supplied from one of the river''s tributaries and entered the city via an aqueduct about 80m above the Tajo [1]. There was a storage system using large cisterns [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
