ted externally by stone walls, which surround a level area some 54 metres in diameter [1]. Its name means \"White Hill Castle\" [1]. Later Neolithic pottery indicates use in this period, and it may have been a henge monument at this time [1]. The earliest bank and ditch belong to the end of the Neolithic period (2500-2000 BC) [1]. During the Iron Age, the present wall was built, and it was rebuilt in Roman times and later [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
