 an archaeological site located in the district of San Isidro, in the city of Lima [1]. It has the form of a truncated stepped pyramid [1]. The first archaeological excavations were carried out in 1942 and were directed by Julio C. Tello, who stated that Huaca Huallamarca\\''s boundaries were marked by the Huatica and Surco canals [1]. Tello also identified three main moments of occupation: from the beginning of the Lima culture period (2nd century BCE to 7th century AD), through the Yshma (11th century AD), to the Inca period (15th–16th centuries AD) [1]. The construction of the Huallamarca pyramid began with the Huallas from 200 BC to AD 200 [1]. Archaeologist Julio C. Tello described Huallamarca as a structure built exclusively with small handmade adobes in the shape of molars or irregular cones [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
