    ('dfd872f8-26e9-446d-936e-bdbcd978257a'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:dfd872f8-26e9-446d-936e-bdbcd978257a:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''8'' restored on Mount Pleasant Henge', '6ff4fe8cee33f460ddcea418079c6a30', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Henge'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 7 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:42218", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0063:chunk-0001: description ''Mount Pleasant is a Neolithic mega-henge enclosure in Dorset, England, southeast of Dorchester in the parish of West Stafford. The egg-shaped enclosure measures approximately 370m along its long axis and dates to around 2500 BC, making it one of five known mega-henges in southern Britain. Rediscovered by Stuart Piggott in 1936 and excavated by Geoffrey Wainwright in 1970-71, the site contained a timber palisade, a large round mound, and concentric timber and stone structures. The adjacent Conquer Barrow rises about 8m high and 30m across.'' -> \"Mount Pleasant henge is a Neolithic henge enclosure in the English county of Dorset [1]. It lies southeast of Dorchester in the civil parish of West Stafford [1]. The enclosure is egg-shaped, measuring 400 yd along its long axis and dates to 2878–2470 cal BC [1]. A geophysical survey in 1969 identified entrances to the henge enclosure and a smaller inner henge enclosure at the south western end of 150 ft diameter [1]. Excavation in the 1960s revealed little material in the henge ditch though some fragments of grooved ware and children''s skeletons were found [1]. The inner enclosure however contained large numbers of postholes [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
