    ('e1b8b97e-0344-4248-8a0f-86d3b956c759'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '4', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:e1b8b97e-0344-4248-8a0f-86d3b956c759:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''4'' restored on Ballyedmonduff Wedge Tomb', '7146ba16be99415ff0a7f42c7b7efb2b', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Tomb'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 3 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28512", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0152:chunk-0001: site_type ''Necropolis/tombs complex'' -> ''Tomb''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:42256", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0064:chunk-0001: description ''Early Bronze Age wedge tomb (c. 2500-2000 BC) on the southeastern slope of Two Rock Mountain in Dun Laoghaire-Rathdown, Ireland, and a National Monument. Regarded as one of the finest examples of its type in Ireland, the burial gallery is aligned east-west and divided into three chambers surrounded by a horseshoe-shaped kerb. Excavations by Sean O Riordain and Ruadhri de Valera uncovered over 140 Beaker pottery sherds, flint, a stone macehead, and cremated human remains. Seven cup marks on a nearby granite rock reflect late Neolithic artistic traditions.'' -> ''The Ballyedmonduff Wedge Tomb is a wedge-shaped gallery grave and a National Monument in Dún Laoghaire–Rathdown, Ireland [1]. Ballyedmonduff Wedge Tomb is found on the south-eastern slope of the Two Rock mountain [1]. The tomb was excavated in the 1830s and then again in the 1940s; during this excavation, cremated bone, a polished stone hammer, flints and pottery were found [1]. The tomb is U-shaped and features double-walling; the rectangular chamber is divided into three parts [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
