atres in the Roman empire [1]. It sat roughly 5,000 spectators [1]. Around 2 BC, the theatre was renovated and presented to the city of Pompeii as a gift by two relatives, M. Holconius Rufus and M. Holconius Celer, according to an inscription in the theatre [1]. The Odeon was a smaller roofed theatre, theatrum tectum, that sat 1500 spectators and was built in 80 BC [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
