    ('e282f2a0-5fbd-445b-81dc-63432936feff'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '7', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:e282f2a0-5fbd-445b-81dc-63432936feff:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''7'' restored on Amazmaz', 'f3459f64a8d5906505c7060662f3bed8', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Rock art'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 5 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:42260", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0064:chunk-0001: description ''An isolated steep-sided elevation on the western Adrar plateau in Mauritania, approximately 400 km northeast of Nouakchott. At its base lie the gueltas of Amazmaz, a chain of rock-sheltered ponds surrounded by rushes that have sustained life for millennia. The slopes above the water feature Neolithic rock paintings, part of a broader Saharan pastoral art tradition (c. 5500-2000 BC) depicting cattle, hunting scenes, and human figures. The Adrar region contains roughly thirty known rock art sites documenting the transition from a wetter Saharan climate to the present desert.'' -> ''Amazmaz is an isolated elevation with steep slopes in the western part of the Adrar plateau in Mauritania, 400 km northeast of the capital Nouakchott [1]. At the foot of the hill there are the gueltas of Amazmaz, a chain of ponds, hidden among rocks and surrounded by rushes, but used for thousands of years, as evidenced by the rock paintings on the slopes bordering the waters [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
