    ('eebdcbf3-42aa-4590-b07e-b3bbe40c309f'::uuid, 'mystery', '9', '8', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:eebdcbf3-42aa-4590-b07e-b3bbe40c309f:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''8'' restored on Aymestrey Burial', 'c7118e1a3ff35f858d8f24b651757430', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 9 from (''Museum'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 2 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43145", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0067:chunk-0001: description ''The Aymestrey burial was a Beaker cist discovered at Aymestrey, Herefordshire, England [1]. The remains and associated objects are now displayed in a recreated cist at Leominster Museum [1][2].'' -> ''The Aymestrey burial was a beaker cist at Aymestrey, Herefordshire, England [1]. While working a gravel quarry at Aymestrey, in June 1987, employees of ARC unearthed a hole with a stone lining, and human remains visible within [1]. They called in archaeologists from Hereford and Worcester County Council, who carried out an excavation and discovered a stone-lined burial pit containing the body of a child, lying on its left-hand side in a foetal position [1]. Alongside the body were an earthenware bell beaker and a flint knife [1]. The burial was dated to the Early Bronze Age [1]. The site lies between the Iron Age hill forts at Pyon Wood and Croft Ambrey, and alongside a tributary of the River Lugg [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
