    ('f5f8472d-d102-48b6-98b3-2d9fcfa53752'::uuid, 'antiquity', '4', '3', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:f5f8472d-d102-48b6-98b3-2d9fcfa53752:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: antiquity ''3'' restored on Castle Ring', 'da69afe80dc0b03e45f66c8737bca7bb', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 4 from period_start -500"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29583", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0309:chunk-0001: period_start ''1'' -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30542", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43203", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0068:chunk-0001: description ''Castle Ring is a multivallate Iron Age hillfort on the southern edge of Cannock Chase in Staffordshire, occupying the highest point at 242 metres elevation. Dating from approximately 500 BC, it was likely built by a local Celtic tribe and abandoned around 43 AD following Roman conquest of the area. The 9-acre fort is defended by two banks and ditches, with a counterscarp bank on the north and west sides, multiple defences to the south-east, and an inturned entrance on the eastern side. It is the best-preserved of eight Iron Age hillforts in Staffordshire. Earthwork remains of a medieval hunting lodge survive within the enclosure, built when Cannock Chase served as a royal hunting ground. The site is a scheduled monument and holds Green Flag Heritage status.'' -> ''Castle Ring is an Iron Age hill fort, situated high up on the southern edge of Cannock Chase, Staffordshire [1]. It is the highest point on The Chase with an elevation of 242 metres [1]. It is near the village of Cannock Wood, south of Rugeley and north of Burntwood [1]. Castle Ring is thought to have first been occupied c. 500 BCE by an Ancient British tribe named the Cornovii [1]. It was abandoned c. 43 CE as a consequence of Romans occupying the area [1]. Apart from perimeter earthworks, little remains visible [1]. Parts of the ground in the ring appear to have been ploughed, but there is no consensus as to whether this was carried out in prehistoric times, or in the medieval period, when a hunting lodge was also built in the ring [1]. The remains of this lodge are still visible [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
