nd the largest in the Balkans [1]. The Roman baths of Varna were built towards the end of the 2nd century and remained in use for about a hundred years, till the late 3rd century [1]. Coins of Roman emperor Septimius Severus (r. 193–211) have been discovered among the bath ruins [1]. The Roman Thermae of Varna feature the whole range of facilities including an apodyterium, a frigidarium, a tepidarium and a caldarium as well as a palaestra [1]. Heating was provided by means of a hypocaust, an underfloor heating system of pipes [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
