    ('feeb5055-f18a-46f3-82cf-fbdfe23d72b4'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '7', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:feeb5055-f18a-46f3-82cf-fbdfe23d72b4:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''7'' restored on Kanichi', 'dcc48bc7c8563f6348de23f969760511', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Necropolis/tombs complex'', ''500 - 1000 AD'') is shared by 5 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:45505", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0114:chunk-0001: description ''Kanichi is an archaeological complex of approximately 200,000 square meters in the Ayacucho Region, Lucanas Province, Peru. The site was influenced by both the Wari (6th-11th century AD) and Chanka cultures and includes chullpas (funerary towers), religious and ceremonial buildings, service centers, and a water system of wells and springs. The complex was declared National Cultural Heritage by RDN No. 197/INC on April 2, 2003.'' -> ''Kanichi is an archaeological site in Peru [1]. Kanichi lies in the Ayacucho Region, Lucanas Province, Carmen Salcedo District [1]. The archaeological complex, which is about 200,000 square meters, was influenced by the Wari and Chanka cultures [1]. The complex includes a variety of buildings including Chullpas, religious and ceremonial buildings, service centers, and a water system of wells and springs [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
