lly revealed and then looted at the beginning of the 20th century [1]. During World War II a bomb caused the partial destruction of its roof and the backfill of the chamber [1]. It is a significant funerary monument excavated in 1966 by the curator Mr. C. Davaras and partly restored in 1970 [1]. A corridor (\"dromos\"), 25.10m long and 1.60m wide, leads to the chamber [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('ff55d038-92b0-4fad-9973-96cab63ec8db'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '3', 'card-stats-2026-09-23-rollback:ff55d038-92b0-4fad-9973-96cab63ec8db:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-09-23: mystery ''3'' restored on Temple of Jupiter, Split', '8721f776358de92d0f5f76a6a2363883', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Temple'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 10 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d65d0c3df8f22029 (2026-09-25 12:21:51.637605+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 2888 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 60048 cells"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28598", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0167:chunk-0001: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''Temple''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:45507", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0114:chunk-0001: description \"The Temple of Jupiter is a 3rd-century Roman temple in Split, Croatia, located in the western part of Diocletian''s Palace near the Peristyle [1]. Built between 295 and 305 AD during the palace''s construction, it was dedicated to the god Jupiter [1]. In the 6th century, the temple was likely converted into the Baptistery of St. John the Baptist, coinciding with the building of a crypt dedicated to St. Thomas [1]. Before the entrance stands one of twelve sphinxes brought from Egypt by Emperor Diocletian [1]. The Scottish architect Robert Adam praised it as one of Europe''s most beautiful monuments [1].\" -> \"The Temple of Jupiter is a temple in Split, Croatia dedicated to the Ancient Roman god Jupiter [1]. It is located in the western part of Diocletian''s Palace near the Peristyle, the central square of the imperial complex [1]. Before the entrance to the Temple is one of the twelve sphinxes brought from Egypt by Emperor Diocletian [1]. The Temple of Jupiter was constructed between 295 and 305 as part of Diocletian''s Palace [1]. Since the Emperor unexpectedly abdicated the throne in 305 and arrived at the palace from Nicomedia earlier, finishing work on the construction of the Palace was stopped so parts of the Temple remained unfinished [1]. Reliefs depicting gods and various heroes, such as Victoria, Triton, Helios, Hercules, Jupiter and Apollo, are placed in front of the Temple, above the entrance [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
